From 1c91ba1a9adbcd9e1eb6c32bdc677265e8012bd3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mukul dhariwal <mukul.dhariwal94@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 7 May 2026 20:23:57 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 8/9] cel: shrink process-wide compile-cache cap to 1500

Heap profiles from a real apiserver (issue-131417, snapshot at 1.7 GB
inuse) show the cel.Program retained per cache entry is ~150-250 KB
once you account for the per-program FunctionDecl.Bindings copy and
the interpreter dispatcher table populated from it. The previous
5000-entry cap was sized against a ~30-200 KB per-program estimate
that pre-dated the apiserver-shaped env (urls/ip/cidr/regex/jsonpatch/
quantity/semver/lists libraries), so in practice the cache could grow
to ~1 GB on its own.

Drop the cap to 1500. At the empirical per-entry cost this caps the
cache footprint at ~300-400 MB. Templated workloads (the case that
benefits most from program-level dedup) only need a few hundred
distinct keys, so the hit rate is preserved.

Pairs with the cel-go shared-dispatcher change, which removes the
bulk of the per-entry retained cost; once that lands the cap can be
revisited upward.
---
 .../pkg/admission/plugin/cel/compile_cache.go         | 11 +++++++----
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/staging/src/k8s.io/apiserver/pkg/admission/plugin/cel/compile_cache.go b/staging/src/k8s.io/apiserver/pkg/admission/plugin/cel/compile_cache.go
index e0453607ad5..be6ebfb31ef 100644
--- a/staging/src/k8s.io/apiserver/pkg/admission/plugin/cel/compile_cache.go
+++ b/staging/src/k8s.io/apiserver/pkg/admission/plugin/cel/compile_cache.go
@@ -37,10 +37,13 @@ func reflectPointer(p *environment.EnvSet) uintptr {
 }
 
 // defaultCompileCacheSize bounds how many distinct compiled CEL programs are
-// kept in the process-wide cache. Each entry holds one cel.Program (typically
-// 30-200 KB), so 5000 entries cap the cache footprint at a few hundred MB
-// even on pathological clusters.
-const defaultCompileCacheSize = 5000
+// kept in the process-wide cache. Empirical apiserver heap profiles put the
+// retained cost of a single cel.Program at ~150-250 KB (the per-program
+// FunctionDecl.Bindings + interpreter Dispatcher copy dominate, see
+// issue-131417). 1500 entries caps the cache footprint at ~300-400 MB on
+// clusters with thousands of distinct expressions while preserving near-
+// optimal hit rates on templated workloads.
+const defaultCompileCacheSize = 1500
 
 var (
 	// globalCompileCache is swapped via atomic.Pointer so the hot path of
